{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"pettish-snippy-rasbora","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nS2-S5 establish registry-backed help, execution, optional capability behavior, and downstream consumers while retaining derived compatibility exports for safe expansion. RP-05 is incomplete while the facade still exposes parallel policy frozensets, explicit dispatch/intercept ladders, or manual census compatibility that future commands can update instead of the registry.\n\n## Approach\nPerform the contract phase after S2-S5 pass.\n\n1. Enumerate every semantic reference and every string-based patch/import of the old policy names and ladder helpers using semantic navigation plus a repository-wide string scan.\n2. Move each remaining consumer to the route/capability APIs and delete the 19 duplicate policy/census objects, explicit intercept selection ladder, derived compatibility exports, and obsolete generator compatibility data.\n3. Preserve specialized handler modules and nested argument parsing; do not fold them into the registry or facade.\n4. Run a whole-route shadow comparison immediately before deletion and fail on any delta except S2's approved top-level help normalization.\n5. Keep `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py`, the new registry modules, and every touched source module below the 800-line cap; use existing call-graph seams and do not create files under 100 lines.\n6. Document the completed migration and code-only back-out. No ticket/event/bridge/binding migration or cleanup runs.\n\nThe positive rationale is to make the registry the only writable command/capability authority. This story removes migration scaffolding rather than adding another feature flag.\n\n## Compatibility and Rollback\nAll hard-won help, mount/init, confirmation/output, bridge vocabulary, optionality, and degraded-mode tests remain authoritative. Exact behavior deltas are limited to the already approved S2 help/overview change. Before contraction, rollback selects derived compatibility exports; after contraction, reverting the code changes restores the pre-RP-05 router because no stored format changed.\n\n## Testing\nRun the focused real subprocess suites for help/mount/argv/output/aliases/retired commands and selected capabilities, the generator and optionality contracts, then the repository lint/type/module-size/complexity gates. Add negative scans proving old policy symbols and retired tokens are absent from shipped code and active docs while compatibility spellings remain only in registered compatibility routes. The full suite is collateral evidence, not a substitute for these behavior-specific oracles.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No shipped source, generator, test, or active documentation reads or patches the retired policy frozensets, intercept ladder, or compatibility census; all command/capability consumers use the registries.\n- [ ] Whole-route shadow comparison reports no unapproved delta in command identity, mount/init, handler argv, confirmation/output, streams, exit codes, aliases, or capability posture.\n- [ ] The approved top-level help/overview behavior and all pre-existing execution/degradation contracts pass through real subprocess and production-path tests after compatibility exports are removed.\n- [ ] Module-size, complexity, lint, and type gates pass with every touched source module below 800 lines and no mechanically split file under 100 lines.\n- [ ] The migration documentation states the completed contract point and code-only rollback, and no persisted ticket/event/bridge/binding format or data is changed.","id":"69d3-3f7a-8deb-46fc","parent_id":"09ae-e827-1cac-452d","priority":1,"tags":["rp05","cli"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-05 S6 — Complete CLI registry cutover and retire duplicate route authorities"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787069647889720001,"uuid":"a4be7d9c-81bb-44ed-8571-38177911276d"}